  "group": "actions-objdiff331-literal-relocations",
  "extent_model": "objdiff-3.3.1-combined",
  "allow_incomplete_unit": true,
  "reason": "objdiff-cli 3.3.1 (sha1 3130e4288d483d259d1588092c8159f8e0230e08) scores these byte-identical data sections below 100% because its data relocation comparator treats the '$' in every MSVC string-literal name (??_C@...?$AA@) as a Metrowerks unique-ID separator, so identical relocation targets compare unequal and fall back to an address test inside objdiff's synthetic combined section, whose COMDAT order differs (docs/objdiff_data_relocation_defect_20260922.md; fixed upstream in 3.6.0). The group holds all 46 target sections of the report sections .data 16 B, .rdata 2,388 B; each is section_infos_equal to the rebuilt object (bytes and relocation addresses, types, destinations and addends) with identical flags, alignment and owner. extent_model objdiff-3.3.1-combined reproduces the reported extents: same-named sections in objdiff order, running offset aligned to max(alignment, 4) after each section, a lone section at its raw size, alignment code 0 = 16 (measured against the frozen 3.3.1 executable on 235 synthetic section tables and on all 833 units of the build report: research/opus_data_verifier_20260925/). objdiff's raw report still lists 4 unmatched function(s), hence allow_incomplete_unit; the entry credits data only. V1 verifier form: the rebuilt object adds 15 select-any COMDAT section(s) to these report sections; each is listed in 'surplus' with a pinned snapshot and earns no credit.  Every member also has an identical section symbol table, COMDAT selection and image-address-resolved relocation list in both objects.",
